            <ArticleTitle>Hypothalamic CRFR1 is essential for HPA axis regulation following chronic stress.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-388</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nn.4491</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis is a pivotal component of an organism's response to stressful challenges, and dysfunction of this neuroendocrine axis is associated with a variety of physiological and psychological pathologies. We found that corticotropin-releasing factor type 1 receptor within the paraventricular nucleus of the hypothalamus is an important central component of hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis regulation that prepares the organism for successive exposure to stressful stimuli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
